                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So, personally, I don't get the hate. I've faced several lags (which, frankly, was actually funny most of the time), but all it cost me is to restart the game, and I don't even own a PC setup, just some huawei laptop thinner than my pinky :^\n\nThe storyline. Oh my God, the storyline. The whole Beholder games series have been my comfort games during the recent year. No matter which one, every part of the franchise had felt so incredibly relatable to me. It hit too close to home every time so perfectly, but that's exactly why i love the game series with my whole heart. Speaking about Beholder 3, it seems a lot of people like to frown upon Kim's arc, I've seen ppl call her queerness \"forced\" and \"performative\". NO ITS NOT?? I'm actually quite pleased that Beholder actuallly managed to encapture the deal of being queer in that type of society/place/whatever. As a part of the community and the subculture, personally, I it felt one heck of a relatable. I love my girl Kim with all my heart, she's a female me, I am male her- whatever, you get it. And it's actually so comforting and fasctinating how Beholder dared to touch on these topics, and do it good. And in this case, it's not \"performance for brownie points\" how ppl put it, it's how many actually live. Besides, queerness in dystopian settings is just another trope to explore, there's so many potential for interesting dynamics. \n\nI lowkey missed the original's soundtracks tho, so I think it wouldn't hurt to put some tributes or easter eggs into Beholder 3 like it was done with Beholder 2 and Conductor. \nI swallowed up the whole game series, and it was a cheif's kiss. I love Beholder with all its flaws, it's my heart and home\n\nI remember being skeptical about buying Beholder 3 due to mix reviews, but in the end, I didn't regret even a second I spent on the walkthrough. If you're also considering trying it out and your device can handle it, I BEG YOU. It's so underrated, I can't stress it enough. A worthy part of a peak franchise. Mwah.",
